{=============================================================================
  Ideal Stirling cycle with a regenerator (exercise)
  CoolSolve Library model CSL-0201
 -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
  Teaching exercise (ULiège MECA0002, session sheet R4bis). Theoretical
  Stirling cycle on ideal-gas Air: isothermal compression and expansion,
  isochoric heat exchange, volumetric compression ratio. An ideal regenerator
  recovers the isochoric heat. Efficiencies with and without that regenerator
  are compared with the Carnot efficiency between the cycle temperature limits.

  Inputs : fluid$, R, r_v, p[1], T[1], T[3]
  Outputs: w_net, q_c, q_couteux, eta_stirling, eta_stirling_regen, eta_carnot
  Units  : SI - temperatures in K, pressures in Pa, energies in J
           (property calls receive °C; the original subtracts 273)
  Source : thermo_models R05_E03_2022.EES (R4bis) - see README.md
=============================================================================}

"Exercise 5. Theoretical Stirling cycle with an ideal regenerator. Minimum pressure and temperature 100 kPa and 25 °C, volumetric compression ratio 10, maximum temperature 1000 °C. Work and heat of each of the four processes, overall efficiency, comparison with the Carnot efficiency between the minimum and maximum temperatures, and the efficiency without the regenerator."

"!Data"

fluid$ = 'Air'                         "ideal-gas Air, the name in the equation window"
R = 287                                "gas constant [J/kg-K]; 0.287 kJ/kg-K in the original"
r_v = 10                               "volumetric compression ratio [-]"
p[1] = 100e3                           "minimum cycle pressure [Pa]; 100 kPa in the original"
T[1] = 298                             "minimum cycle temperature [K]; 25 °C written as 298 K"
T[3] = 1273                            "maximum cycle temperature [K]; 1000 °C written as 1273 K"

"!Solution"

"!Isothermal compression 1-2: T constant; heat is removed from the fluid during the compression"
v[1] = R*T[1]/p[1]                     "specific volume at 1 from the ideal-gas law [m^3/kg]"

T[2] = T[1]                            "isothermal process [K]"
v[2] = v[1]/r_v                        "specific volume at 2 from the volumetric ratio [m^3/kg]"
p[2] = R*T[2]/v[2]                     "pressure at 2 from the ideal-gas law [Pa]"

w_12 = R*T[1]*ln(r_v)                  "work required by the compression: -integral of p dv [J/kg]"
w_12 + q_12 = cv12*(T[2]-T[1])         "first law, for the heat exchanged: q + w = delta u [J/kg]"
cv12 = cv(fluid$,T=(T[1]+T[2])/2-273)  "cv of Air at the mean temperature of 1-2 [J/kg-K]; T[] is K, the call takes °C"

"!Isochoric heating 2-3: v constant"
"!This heat, equal to q_41 in absolute value, can be recovered with a regenerator"
v[3] = v[2]                            "isochoric process [m^3/kg]"
w_23 = 0                               "work is zero for an isochoric process: -integral of p dv = 0 [J/kg]"
w_23 + q_23 = cv23*(T[3]-T[2])         "heat from the first law [J/kg]"
p[3] = R*T[3]/v[3]                     "pressure at 3 from the ideal-gas law [Pa]"
cv23 = cv(fluid$,T=(T[2]+T[3])/2-273)  "cv of Air at the mean temperature of 2-3 [J/kg-K]; T[] is K, the call takes °C"

"!Isothermal expansion 3-4: T constant; heat is added to the fluid"
T[4] = T[3]                            "isothermal process [K]"
p[4] = R*T[4]/v[4]                     "specific volume at 4 is known below; pressure from the ideal-gas law [Pa]"
w_34 = R*T[3]*ln(v[3]/v[4])            "work of the isothermal expansion: -integral of p dv [J/kg]"
w_34 + q_34 = cv34*(T[4]-T[3])         "heat received during the expansion, from the first law [J/kg]"
cv34 = cv(fluid$,T=(T[3]+T[4])/2-273)  "cv of Air at the mean temperature of 3-4 [J/kg-K]; T[] is K, the call takes °C"

"!Isochoric cooling 4-1: v constant"
v[4] = v[1]                            "specific volume at 4 [m^3/kg]"
w_41 = 0                               "work is zero for an isochoric process [J/kg]"
w_41 + q_41 = cv41*(T[1]-T[4])         "heat from the first law [J/kg]"
cv41 = cv(fluid$,T=(T[1]+T[4])/2-273)  "cv of Air at the mean temperature of 4-1 [J/kg-K]; T[] is K, the call takes °C"

"!Thermal efficiency"

"!Without a regenerator both heats must be supplied: q_23 during the isochoric heating and q_34 during the isothermal expansion"
eta_stirling = w_net/q_couteux         "efficiency without regenerator [-]"
w_net = -(w_34+w_12)                   "net work, the useful effect [J/kg]"
q_couteux = q_23+q_34                  "heat that must be supplied without a regenerator [J/kg]"
"!With a regenerator only q_34 is supplied during the isothermal expansion. The isochoric heat q_23 is recovered from the isochoric cooling q_41"
eta_stirling_regen = w_net/q_c         "efficiency with the ideal regenerator [-]"
q_c = q_34                             "heat supplied with the regenerator [J/kg]"
"!Carnot efficiency. The cold source is at T[1] and the hot source at T[3]"
eta_carnot = 1-T[1]/T[3]               "Carnot efficiency between the cycle temperature limits [-]"

"!With the regenerator the theoretical Stirling efficiency equals the Carnot efficiency. Without the regenerator it is about 55 percent of the Carnot efficiency."

s[1] = entropy('Air',T=T[1]-273,p=p[1])  "specific entropy at 1 [J/kg-K]; T[] is K, p[] is Pa"
s[2] = entropy('Air',T=T[2]-273,p=p[2])  "specific entropy at 2 [J/kg-K]"
s[3] = entropy('Air',T=T[3]-273,p=p[3])  "specific entropy at 3 [J/kg-K]"
s[4] = entropy('Air',T=T[4]-273,p=p[4])  "specific entropy at 4 [J/kg-K]"
